sted set, never add a candidate. Effective requirement is a gate, not a build input (same reasoning that excluded capability evidence in decision 0006); no bypass because Stage A precedes cache lookup. Result: zero frozen artifacts change and adopting the contract causes no rebuild. Go costs no new process - Stage A reuses the three existing package-independent bootstrap probes, so the five Go argument-vector forms stay five and manager-worker-v1 is untouched.\n\nStated asymmetry: a descriptor requirement is unreadable at Stage A because the descriptor arrives with the repository, so Stage A gates on baseline INTERSECT manifest and the descriptor requirement joins at Stage B. That is why the consuming-manifest requirement is REQUIRED in the next schema.\n\nGates, standalone, real exit codes - validate 0 (42 schemas / 422 vector files, before and after), python unittest 0 (29 tests), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0 no output, git diff --check 0, generate-vectors 0. Regenerated conformance/v1 and release/1.0.0-rc.5.json are byte-identical to the accepted predecessor. Clean git-init probe: regenerate-check x2 = 0, release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5 = 0. Two negative probes expected-red and red: retired descriptor stem in the new doc rejected by validate (exit 1), broken local link in decision 0007 rejected by validate (exit 1); both reverted, final validate 0. Note: make regenerate-check cannot pass inside the task worktree because it diffs against 57c1f56 while the rc.5 candidate is uncommitted - determinism proven by predecessor byte-comparison and the clean probe instead.\n\nDeliberately not done: no protocol/profile/SECURITY/schema/vector change (TASK-260728-2jaw7h), no schema version numbers (TASK-260728-2spy93), no README release-table row (would falsely claim the design is part of the rc.5 specification set), and no invented probe argv or normalization for rust/swift/kotlin/jdk (needs a qualified host).\n\nReviewer focus: is the filter-never-select claim airtight across manifest, descriptor and every stage-B metadata source; is Stage A movement genuinely gate-neutral; is excluding the effective requirement from the cache key correct given Stage A precedes lookup; are the reserved obligation lists complete enough that downstream driver decisions cannot reopen selection; does prerelease rejection break a case worth admitting.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-af7289, pid=8002, exit=0)\nReviewer focus: treat this as the research/design contract whose normative schema/vector landing is explicitly TASK-260728-2jaw7h. Independently challenge whether constraints can only filter manager-trusted candidates; Stage A ordering is truly before acquisition/cache/mutation without dropping required predecessors; Stage B cannot bypass source validation/audit; descriptor asymmetry is fail-closed; prerelease/version intersection is deterministic; package data cannot select path/URL/channel/install/env/trust; guidance is manager-owned primary-source text/URL only and v1 cannot auto-install. Verify whether excluding the effective requirement and guidance catalog from cache identity is sound while resolved toolchain identities remain bound, and whether reserved Rust/Swift/Kotlin/JDK obligations are sufficient for downstream work. Re-run docs/link/retired-name and unchanged rc.5 release gates; no stage, commit, publish, pin advance, or platform claim.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-e30a89, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-e30a89)\nReviewer verdict: changes requested and routed to analysis. Evidence is attached as TASK-260728-1g0z69_review-verdict.md. Blocking issues: preserve the existing manager-tested Go release-family allowlist; make guidance coverage total for all eleven diagnostics; make guidance IDs compatible with supersession; remove the package-channel diagnostic contradiction; and correct the cache vector so current incompatibility fails before lookup rather than rebuilding.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-e30a89, pid=13554, exit=0)\nRework cycle 1, blocking reviewer findings: (1) preserve the existing Go manager-tested-release-family gate by adding a manager-owned closed compatibility set/predicate to each registry entry, evaluating it in Stage A with deterministic diagnostic/guidance and preserve/reject vectors; at_least alone must not admit unknown Go 1.99. (2) Make guidance total over all 11 diagnostics with an explicit code-to-reason mapping, including requirement_invalid, requirement_unsatisfiable, version_undetermined, package_influence_forbidden, and changed. (3) Make guidance_id lifecycle implementable by adding immutable revision/generation or otherwise defining distinct valid IDs and superseded_by semantics. (4) Resolve channel contradiction: distinguish forbidden package-selected install/toolchain channels from source metadata channel assertions, define precedence and deterministic positive/negative vectors. (5) Correct vector 35: incompatible current resolved toolchain fails before cache lookup; only a compatible current toolchain with a different cached toolchain identity causes cache miss/rebuild. Update decision, reference and evidence, rerun all unchanged-rc.5/links/negative/release gates, and hand off for another independent review. Preserve the task worktree and do not stage, commit, publish, pin, or claim platform validation.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-e41666, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-e41666)\nRework cycle 1 complete: all five blocking reviewer findings addressed in the same task worktree /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1g0z69/curator-spec-worktree. Delta versus the accepted predecessor is still exactly decisions/0007-compiled-build-toolchain-preflight.md, docs/compiled-build-toolchain-requirements.md, one CHANGELOG bullet. Nothing staged, committed, published, pinned; no platform validation claimed. Predecessor TASK-260728-2kp3tv worktree preserved read-only (127 dirty entries at 57c1f56, nothing staged).\n\n(1) Go family gate preserved. New REQUIRED registry field compatibility: a closed manager-owned set of tested release families matched by exact set membership, never ordering. go = {(1,23)}, carrying profiles/manager.md 2.2 forward unchanged. Independent of the requirement - a constraint can neither widen nor narrow it and nothing on the wire surface reaches it. New twelfth diagnostic build_toolchain_untested_release carrying the admitted family set. Stage A gains step 7 with fixed precedence: Go 1.22.0 -> incompatible (step 6), Go 1.99.0 -> untested_release (step 7), so at_least alone admits nothing. Vectors 7 preserve, 31 reject, 32 precedence, 57 identical cache key.\n\n(2) Guidance totality mechanical. reason is exactly the diagnostic code suffix, so the code-to-reason mapping is the identity and stays total as codes are added; the five uncovered reasons plus untested_release are covered. New guidance_class (host/configuration/authoring) fixes the admissible primary_source origin per class, which is what makes authoring and configuration reasons carriable at all - the language official origin, the manager operator documentation, or this specification, all manager-trusted.