es (requirement-only admissibility, package-reachable family set, blanket channel prohibition, tuple-only guidance IDs, host-only guidance reasons) and states that no currently admitted Go release becomes inadmissible and none currently rejected becomes admissible.\n\nGates, standalone, real exit codes: validate 0 (42 schemas / 422 vector files), python unittest 0 (29 tests), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0 no output, git diff --check 0, generate-vectors 0. Regenerated conformance/v1 and release/1.0.0-rc.5.json byte-identical to the accepted predecessor. Clean git-init probe at 1b02fa0: regenerate-check x2 = 0, release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5 = 0. Two negative probes against the reworked files expected-red and red: retired descriptor stem rejected by validate (exit 1), broken local link rejected by validate (exit 1); both reverted, final validate 0. make regenerate-check still cannot pass inside the task worktree because it diffs against 57c1f56 with the rc.5 candidate uncommitted - determinism proven by predecessor byte-comparison and the clean probe instead. Python gates run with the existing validation-venv because ambient python3 lacks jsonschema.\n\nReviewer focus for this cycle: does compatibility fully restore manager.md 2.2 and is requirement-before-compatibility the right precedence; is the 3.1 surface split a real distinction rather than a relabeling; is channel=stable permitted rather than mismatched correct (the one place this cycle relaxes previous text); do the identity code-to-reason mapping and guidance_class keep primary_source honest for authoring/configuration reasons; is the revisioned ID plus one-active-per-tuple sufficient for TASK-260728-ypbuav; does splitting old vector 35 into positive 14 and negative 45 leave any cache-versus-fail-fast case unstated.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-e41666, pid=17140, exit=0)\nReview cycle 2 focus: independently verify each prior blocking finding is closed, not merely restated. In particular, Go 1.99 must fail the manager-owned exact tested-family compatibility predicate despite satisfying at_least; pre-baseline precedence must be deterministic; all 12 diagnostics must have a total valid guidance mapping; revisioned guidance IDs must permit immutable supersession and one active tuple; invalid declared ids must still resolve guidance safely; manifest/descriptor channels remain forbidden while source metadata compared fields can never select/activate a toolchain and forbidden fields win; current incompatibility never reaches cache while differing compatible toolchain identity is a miss/rebuild. Challenge whether stable source channel acceptance and guidance primary-source classes preserve trust. Re-run unchanged rc.5, deterministic, link, retired-name and release gates. No edits, stage, commit, publish, pin or platform claim by reviewer.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-092e80, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-092e80)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-092e80, pid=29455, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 2 directive 2026-07-28: queued for the first free Claude Opus 5 producer slot; continue only in the existing task-owned curator-spec worktree and preserve the accepted predecessor read-only. Close all four cycle-2 blockers from TASK-260728-1g0z69_review-verdict-cycle-2.md: (1) make the complete Go metadata classifier exhaustive over every officially admitted ToolchainName class, including toolchain default, canonical release names, and custom/non-canonical names, with deterministic outcomes and focused vector